.env.local

# Demo builds. `vite build --mode demo` reads .env.demo instead of .env.production, which
# is how the marketing screenshots are taken: with no Supabase URL or key the app falls
# back to browser storage, so a throwaway book can be loaded without touching anyone's
# real data. The file only holds empty values, but an env file in the repo is how a build
# quietly picks up the wrong configuration later.
.env.demo
dist-demo/
